Package: zisar
Title: Zero-Inflated Spatial Autoregressive Models for Count Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Niccolò", "Salvini", , "niccolo@binoocle.net", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Giuseppe", "Arbia", role = "aut"),
    person("Vincenzo", "Nardelli", role = "aut")
  )
Description: Fits the zero-inflated spatial autoregressive (ZISAR) model for
    spatial count data with excess zeros. A simultaneous autoregressive (SAR)
    process on the latent log-mean of a zero-inflated negative binomial
    model carries spatial spillovers, and unit-level Gaussian random effects
    absorb residual heterogeneity. An optional second SAR field in the
    zero-inflation predictor captures spatially clustered structural zeros.
    Parameters are estimated by maximising
    the Laplace approximation to the marginal likelihood with 'TMB', whose
    automatic differentiation and sparse matrix algebra make tens of
    thousands of spatial units feasible. Methods are provided for direct,
    indirect and total marginal effects, counterfactual prediction,
    residuals and simulation from the model.
